    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nMore `runtime/` should be owned by lua (< is this still up to debate?). Much of this is gradual increments (i.e. builtin plugins) but ftplugin *would* be an easy place to start.\n\nLooking for broader input after [this comment](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40723#issuecomment-4962668083) and [this one](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40723#issuecomment-4964287557).\n\n#33160 *may* be blocking? We'd hypothetically use `vim.b.undo_ftplugin`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAll ftplugins in lua, avoiding weirdness like https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40709\n\nOnce again, maybe this shouldn't happen - just looking to collect opinions.\n\n@clason @justinmk \n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-14T08:34:00Z",
    "closed_by": {
