            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ftplugin is an easy place to start en masse\n\nI *would* be excited if ftplugins got rewritten in Lua, but there needs to be focus to it. This would be a large task, and definitely not easy.\n\nFor example, a longstanding issue I've had with Vim's ftplugins is that a lot of them set options which should really be left alone for the user to decide. One example is ftplugins setting 'tabstop' and 'expandtab' together, enforcing a preferred tab size for no reason (compare to `:h editorconfig.indent_size`, which functions much more rationally). Another example is 'formatoptions' ([vim/vim#16657](https://github.com/vim/vim/issues/16657)), which (imo) is much too opinionated to be set by ftplugins at all.\n\nThen there's security. Vim's ftplugins are relatively insecure, to the point that it makes 'modeline' insecure; see #39044.\n\nIMO, for this to be worth it, every single ftplugin would basically need to be ported from scratch, not just converted to Lua with no changes, [and definitely not using AI to do it in large batches](https://matrix.to/#/!HCjHPBLFfoFpYNgwdE:matrix.org/$uu0cwAfDlH-lrGUCxhjx3tLckfAnmTru2ywZTKqr0ZM?via=mozilla.org&via=matrix.org&via=unredacted.org).",
